Appendix F — Profiling protocol and stationarity (Gate 3, Proposition 2)

F.1 Metrics

K_{\text{read}} and K_{\text{write}} are instantiated as dram__bytes_read.sum and dram__bytes_write.sum. K_{\text{total}} is their sum over the decode kernels. L_{\text{KV}} is computed from the workload parameters via the formula in §1.4.

F.2 Replay modes and cache control

· Arm \mathcal{B}: default cache control, kernel replay. Deterministic counters, but cold-cache.
· Arm \mathcal{B}': --replay-mode application --cache-control none. Application replay, no explicit flush, caches primed by the application.

Cache control is independent of replay mode and must be disabled explicitly. Disabling cache control can improve performance and better replicate application behaviour when cache priming is part of the measured workload, but it can produce incorrect results for multi-pass metrics. Arm \mathcal{B}' is therefore a diagnostic for K, not a replacement for \mathcal{B}.

F.3 Stationarity ratio

For treatment level z,

\rho_z^{\mathcal{B}}=\frac{K^{\mathcal{B}}_{\text{profiled}}(z)}{L_{\text{KV}}(z)},
\qquad
\rho_z^{\mathcal{B}'}=\frac{K^{\mathcal{B}'}_{\text{profiled}}(z)}{L_{\text{KV}}(z)}.

F.4 Decision rule

The stationarity gate passes if and only if

\frac{\rho_1^{\mathcal{B}}}{\rho_0^{\mathcal{B}}}\in[\underline{\rho}^{\text{pre}},\overline{\rho}^{\text{pre}}]
\quad\text{and}\quad
\frac{\rho_z^{\mathcal{B}'}}{\rho_z^{\mathcal{B}}}\in[\underline{\rho}'^{\text{pre}},\overline{\rho}'^{\text{pre}}]
\ \text{for each }z.

Both bands are derived from pilot variance and pre-registered. If the second condition fails, the arms are not merged and Gate 3 fails regardless of \|\Delta K\|.

