☐ Hardware SKU, driver version, and CUDA version recorded per run.
☐ Direct nvmlDeviceGetTotalEnergyConsumption support query logged.
☐ Counter resolution and estimated update interval reported, stratified by hardware class.
☐ Known-load validation discrepancy reported.
☐ Gate −1, Gate 0, Gate 1, Gate 2, Gate 3, Gate 4 verdicts recorded per treatment.
☐ Kernel-family identity \kappa and regime vector r recorded per run.
☐ Profiling arm (\mathcal{B} or \mathcal{B}') recorded per traffic measurement.
☐ Stationarity ratios \rho_z^{\mathcal{B}}, \rho_z^{\mathcal{B}'} and bands reported.
☐ First-stage F_{\text{fs}} reported with the pre-registered threshold.
☐ Anderson–Rubin interval reported when F_{\text{fs}} is marginal.
☐ Block-level resampling seed and resample count recorded.
☐ Thermal-clock gate thresholds, observed temperature and clock variances, and throttle bits recorded.
☐ Pre-registration document archived and timestamped before the main phase.
☐ Law-consistency inputs (\hat\beta_{KV}, \Delta K, \Delta E, \delta_{\text{law}}) recorded with the verdict.

The checklist is a reporting obligation, not a guarantee of identification. Passing every item does not convert a bundle treatment into a clean one, and failing any item does not by itself invalidate the total-effect estimate.

